---
// Studio Dentistico Pieri: a full, public case study (my own client, not Capgemini).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseIntro from '../../components/CaseIntro.astro';
import DeviceDuo from '../../components/DeviceDuo.astro';
import PhoneCarousel from '../../components/PhoneCarousel.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url.js';

const phones = [
  ['mob-index', 'Home on mobile: the three dentists, the title and the booking buttons.'],
  ['mob-services', 'What we do: the list of treatments and the "What do you need?" cards, in plain words.'],
  ['mob-tech', 'Technology for more comfortable care: the intraoral scanner, digital X-rays and training.'],
  ['mob-reviews', 'What patients say: five-star Google reviews.'],
  ['mob-booking', 'Book your first visit: call or WhatsApp, address and opening hours.'],
];
---
<Base title="Studio Dentistico Pieri: designed and coded with Claude in two days · Francesca Folkmer"
  description="A full redesign for a family dental practice in Genoa, designed and coded with Claude in two days: one clear way to book, a first-visit page, treatments in plain words and a practice you can trust.">
  <article class="container case">
    <CaseIntro
      tags={['Healthcare', 'Website', 'End-to-end', 'AI Workflow']}
      title="Studio Dentistico Pieri: designed and coded with Claude, live in two days"
      facts={[['Timeline', '2 days, from the first file to launch'], ['Role', 'Solo, from content audit to code'], ['Built with', 'Claude, for design and code']]}
    >
      <Fragment slot="media"><div class="pieri-cover"><DeviceDuo desktop="/img/pieri/desk-index.webp" mobile="/img/pieri/mob-index.webp"><span slot="back" class="pieri-cover__word">StudioPieri</span></DeviceDuo></div></Fragment>
      <p>A family dental practice in Genoa asked for a <b>deep redesign</b>. I did it on my own, with <b>Claude</b> at every step: content, structure, visual direction and code. <b>Two days</b> from the first file to a live site.</p>
    </CaseIntro>

    <section class="split reveal" aria-labelledby="problem">
      <div class="split__text">
        <div class="split__title">
          <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
          <h2 id="problem" class="h2">Good dentists, a site that didn't show it</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <ul>
            <li><b>Booking was confusing:</b> a form and four different contacts. Which one do you use?</li>
            <li><b>Treatments were unclear:</b> technical names, little explanation.</li>
            <li><b>The family was missing:</b> nothing said it's a small practice run by a family.</li>
            <li><b>No signs of trust:</b> no reviews, no feedback, little about who the dentists are.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split__media"><img class="shot" src={url('/img/pieri/old-site.webp')} alt="The old site: a dark page with a small logo, a blue booking bar and long blocks of small text about the practice's story." loading="lazy" /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="duet reveal" aria-labelledby="duet">
      <div class="split__title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Working with Claude</p>
        <h2 id="duet" class="h2">I directed, Claude built</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="duet__lead">Every design choice was mine. I chose the pages, the content and the look, and wrote the rules. Claude turned them into a design system and code, page by page. I checked every step, on desktop and on mobile.</p>
      <div class="duet__cards">
        <div class="duet__card">
          <h3 class="h4">What I did</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A set of dedicated skills for Claude: accessibility, tone of voice, content</li>
            <li>The pages, and what goes into each one</li>
            <li>The visual direction. Figma was only for sketching, like pen and paper</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="duet__card duet__card--dark">
          <h3 class="h4">What Claude did</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A design system</li>
            <li>The pages, following my rules</li>
            <li>The code: plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript</li>
            <li>SEO</li>
            <li>Hosting and domain</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="decisions" aria-labelledby="decisions">
      <div class="split__title reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Key decisions</p>
        <h2 id="decisions" class="h2">Five things I focused on</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="split reveal">
        <div class="split__text">
          <div class="split__title"><p class="decision__n" aria-hidden="true">01</p><h3 class="h3">A family, and a place you can trust</h3></div>
          <p>Father, son and daughter, in the same practice since 1992. That's the strongest thing they have, and the old site never said it. Now it's the first thing you see: the three of them, smiling, in their own studio. Real photos of the people and the rooms show what it is: a small, calm place where someone knows your name.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split__media stack">
          <img class="shot" src={url('/img/pieri/family-hero.webp')} alt="The new home: the three dentists smiling in their studio, the title 'Il dentista di famiglia a Genova, dal 1992' and the booking buttons." loading="lazy" />
          <img class="stack__card stack__card--a" src={url('/img/pieri/doc-lorenzo.webp')} alt="Dentist card: Dott. Lorenzo Pieri, prosthetics, implants and oral surgery." loading="lazy" />
          <img class="stack__card stack__card--b" src={url('/img/pieri/doc-arianna.webp')} alt="Dentist card: Dott.ssa Arianna Pieri, orthodontics, children and whitening." loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="split split--media-first reveal">
        <div class="split__text">
          <div class="split__title"><p class="decision__n" aria-hidden="true">02</p><h3 class="h3">Booking comes first</h3></div>
          <p>One way to book, said clearly: WhatsApp or a call. And an answer to the question everyone has: "you'll usually get your first appointment within the week". On mobile, Call and WhatsApp stay at the bottom of every page.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split__media"><img class="shot" src={url('/img/pieri/booking.webp')} alt="Booking section: 'Prenota una visita', with phone, WhatsApp and email cards and when you get the first appointment." loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <div class="split reveal">
        <div class="split__text">
          <div class="split__title"><p class="decision__n" aria-hidden="true">03</p><h3 class="h3">A page for the first visit</h3></div>
          <p>The main use case is someone who has never been there and doesn't know what to expect. The new page walks them through it: how the visit works, step by step, how long it takes, what to bring, children, urgent cases.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split__media"><img class="shot" src={url('/img/pieri/first-visit.webp')} alt="First visit page: the promise 'Nessuna cura parte senza il tuo sì' and the four steps of the visit: welcome, check-up, explanation, estimate." loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <div class="split split--media-first reveal">
        <div class="split__text">
          <div class="split__title"><p class="decision__n" aria-hidden="true">04</p><h3 class="h3">Treatments in plain words</h3></div>
          <p>Patients don't search for "pedodonzia": they search for a dentist for their kids. Each treatment now has a plain name first, the technical one beside it, and who in the team takes care of it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split__media"><img class="shot" src={url('/img/pieri/treatments.webp')} alt="Two treatment groups: check-up and cleaning, and children, each with plain names, technical terms in brackets and the dentist in charge." loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <div class="split reveal">
        <div class="split__text">
          <div class="split__title"><p class="decision__n" aria-hidden="true">05</p><h3 class="h3">Proof that they're reliable</h3></div>
          <p>Trust needs proof. The Google rating and the patients' reviews, the technology they use, the year they opened and the happy smiles: each one placed on the page where people make their choice. It helps patients, and it helps search engines too.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="split__media stack">
          <img class="shot" src={url('/img/pieri/reviews.webp')} alt="Reviews section: 'Cosa dicono i pazienti', four five-star Google reviews." loading="lazy" />
          <img class="stack__strip" src={url('/img/pieri/facts.webp')} alt="Key facts: open since 1992, 3 dentists, all ages, 5.0 on Google with 36 reviews." loading="lazy" />
          <img class="stack__card stack__card--tech" src={url('/img/pieri/tech.webp')} alt="Technology section: intraoral scanner, digital X-rays and continuous training." loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mobile reveal" aria-labelledby="mobile">
      <div class="split__title">
        <p class="eyebrow">On mobile</p>
        <h2 id="mobile" class="h2">Booking is always one tap away</h2>
      </div>
      <PhoneCarousel browser label="Studio Pieri on mobile" screens={phones.map(([img, alt]) => [`/img/pieri/${img}.webp`, alt])} />
    </section>

    <section class="final reveal" aria-labelledby="final">
      <h2 id="final" class="h2">Curious to see the final result?</h2>
      <a class="roll" href="https://www.studiodentisticopieri.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span>Visit the live site<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></span>
        <span class="roll__ball" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={22} /></span>
      </a>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* cover: the devices on the navy of the site's booking banner */
  /* cover: the dark navy of the site's footer (#020b26) */
  .pieri-cover { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 4% 6%; border-radius: inherit; overflow: hidden; container-type: size; background: #020b26; }
  /* the big faded wordmark with its line, as in the site's footer */
  .pieri-cover__word { position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: 3%; transform: translateX(-50%); padding-bottom: 2cqw; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14); white-space: nowrap; font-size: 22cqw; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.06em; line-height: .8; color: rgba(255,255,255,.07); user-select: none; z-index: 0; }
  /* the devices always fit inside the cover, whole */
  .pieri-cover :global(.duo) { width: min(100cqw, 100cqh * 1600 / 950); height: auto; }
  .shot { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border-radius: var(--radius-l); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line); }

  /* What I did: five square cards; a carousel on mobile */
  /* Working with Claude: two cards (me / Claude) and the list of cuts */
  .duet { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-block); }
  .duet__lead { max-width: 760px; font-size: var(--fs-lead); }
  .duet__cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  .duet__card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; padding: var(--space-inset); border-radius: var(--radius-l); background: var(--surface); }
  .duet__card--dark { background: var(--night); color: var(--on-night); }
  .duet ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .duet__card ul { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .duet__card--dark ul { color: var(--night-soft); }

  .decisions { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-section); }
  .decisions > .split__title { margin-bottom: calc(var(--space-block) - var(--space-section)); }
  .decision__n { font-size: var(--fs-h2); font-weight: 500; color: var(--sage); line-height: 1; }

  /* an image with smaller cards laid over it */
  .stack { position: relative; padding-bottom: 12%; }
  .stack__card { position: absolute; width: 26%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-l); box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(18,22,20,.22); }
  .stack__card--a { right: 18%; bottom: 0; }
  .stack__card--b { right: -2%; bottom: 6%; }
  .stack__card--tech { width: 46%; right: -2%; bottom: 0; }
  .stack__strip { position: absolute; left: -2%; top: -6%; width: 64%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-l); box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(18,22,20,.18); }

  .mobile { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-block); }
  .final { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-block); text-align: center; }


  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .duet__cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    /* images take less height on small screens */
    .split__media .shot { max-height: 260px; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; }
    .stack { padding-bottom: 16%; }
    .stack .shot { max-height: 220px; }
    .stack__card { width: 30%; }
    .stack__card--tech { width: 44%; }
  }
</style>

